    "answer": {
      "short": "$a\\approx8.00\\text{ cm}$, $b\\approx12.25\\text{ cm}$, $c\\approx15.75\\text{ cm}$.\n\nUse $a:b:c=\\sin30^\\circ:\\sin50^\\circ:\\sin100^\\circ$ and the perimeter to find the common scale.",
      "worked": "The sine rule gives\n$$\\frac{a}{\\sin30^\\circ}=\\frac{b}{\\sin50^\\circ}=\\frac{c}{\\sin100^\\circ}=k.$$\nThus $a=k\\sin30^\\circ$, $b=k\\sin50^\\circ$ and $c=k\\sin100^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}a+b+c&=36\\\\k(\\sin30^\\circ+\\sin50^\\circ+\\sin100^\\circ)&=36\\\\k&=\\frac{36}{\\sin30^\\circ+\\sin50^\\circ+\\sin100^\\circ}\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the exact expression for $k$:\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=\\frac{36\\sin30^\\circ}{\\sin30^\\circ+\\sin50^\\circ+\\sin100^\\circ}\\\\a&\\approx8.00\\text{ cm}\\\\b&=\\frac{36\\sin50^\\circ}{\\sin30^\\circ+\\sin50^\\circ+\\sin100^\\circ}\\\\b&\\approx12.25\\text{ cm}\\\\c&=\\frac{36\\sin100^\\circ}{\\sin30^\\circ+\\sin50^\\circ+\\sin100^\\circ}\\\\c&\\approx15.75\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$\nAll lengths are correct to two decimal places.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
